{
  "abstract": "Four existence theorems on unit fractions, each checked by the Lean kernel from an explicit or implicit witness. (1) An all-odd Giuga sequence: 26 odd integers with Σ1/x − 1/∏x = 1 (Borwein–Borwein–Borwein–Girgensohn 1996, Problem 3). (2) Pairwise-coprime integers > 1 with Σ1/x + 1/∏x = 2, for which Brenton–Hill (1988) wrote \"no solution is known\". (3) A Giuga sequence of value 2 (BBBG Problem 7). (4) Two distinct Giuga sequences with the same product (BBBG Problem 8). Results 2–4 come from one 830-step implicit chain whose elements are too large to write down; it is certified by a residue checker proved sound in Lean. Production: the results, the search programs and this Lean formalization were produced by AI agents (Claude, Anthropic) in a project run by Doug Phillips. He set the goals, directed the work and is responsible for this entry, but he did not independently verify the mathematics. Correctness of the stated theorems rests on the kernel checks recorded here. No human mathematician has yet reviewed the work.",
